# Trivy ignore file - each entry must carry a justification.

# DS-0031 "Possible exposure of secret env in ENV" on pipeline/Dockerfile.
#
# False positive. The check is a name-based heuristic and matches
# PIPELINE_CREDENTIALS_MODE because the identifier contains "CREDENTIALS".
# The variable holds no secret: its only value is the literal string "default",
# a mode flag telling scripts/_common.py to use the ambient ECS task role
# credential chain instead of a named AWS CLI profile (see _common.py
# _use_default_credentials). No credential material is passed via ENV or
# build-args anywhere in this image - the task obtains credentials at runtime
# from the ECS task role.
DS-0031

# DS-0026 "No HEALTHCHECK defined" on pipeline/Dockerfile.
#
# Not applicable. A Docker HEALTHCHECK monitors a long-running service. This
# image is a one-shot batch task: the refresh Step Functions state machine runs
# it to completion and branches on the task exit code, and pipeline_entrypoint.py
# emits per-stage markers plus a non-zero exit on the first failing stage. A
# HEALTHCHECK would add no signal that the state machine does not already have.
DS-0026
